{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StudioPanelDeployChecklist",
  "$description": "The deploy checklist, drawn above the Activity feed in the Bottom dock's Activity tab: what is MISSING before this project can ship, as one row with the chain of prerequisites under it. `publish/deploy-checklist.ts` owns the chain — which link is forged, which is merely unasked, and which command forges the next one — and hands this document a row, four steps and at most one action. Nothing here reads source control, the project config or the command registry. It draws in the Activity tab's own vocabulary because a deploy is an ordered list of stages that finish, which is exactly what a row of that feed already is; a fifth visual idiom for it would be a second design of a thing the tab has.",
  "tagName": "div",
  "attributes": {
    "part": "checklist"
  },
  "style": {
    "$description": "What `.activity-list`, `.activity-row`, `.activity-row--running`, `.activity-row--done`, `.activity-icon`, `.activity-body`, `.activity-head`, `.activity-title`, `.activity-source`, `.activity-status`, `.activity-steps`, `.activity-step`, `.activity-step--done` and `.activity-step-icon` said in `styles/panels.css`, keyed on `part`. This is the LAST reader of those rules — `surfaces/panel-activity.json` carried its own copy when the feed converted, and left the stylesheet standing because this file still drew from it — so the whole `.problem-*, .activity-*` block is dead once this lands. Three token names could not travel: `--spectrum-font-size-50`, `--spectrum-font-size-75` and `--spectrum-corner-radius-75` resolve only inside `<sp-theme>`, and a document mounted into the dock body is outside it, so each would silently have taken its hard-coded px fallback. They are the kit's own scale here. One thing changed meaning on purpose: the step's `data-state` is the checklist's own three-valued state rather than the two CSS classes it used to collapse into, so `unknown` — \"nobody has asked\" — is a state the styling can tell apart from `todo` the day it should.",
    "display": "block",
    "minWidth": "0",
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "color": "var(--fg)",
    "& [part=\"list\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-1)",
      "margin": "0",
      "padding": "0",
      "listStyle": "none"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"]": {
      "$description": "The left border is the state, at 3px, which is the one thing that must be legible without reading the row. Its default is the dim foreground so a state nobody has a colour for still draws a border rather than a gap.",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "flex-start",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-2)",
      "padding": "6px var(--jx-space-2)",
      "border": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "borderLeft": "3px solid var(--fg-dim)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "background": "var(--bg-panel)",
      "color": "var(--fg)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-state=\"running\"]": {
      "borderLeftColor": "var(--accent)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-state=\"done\"]": {
      "borderLeftColor": "var(--success)"
    },
    "& [part=\"state-icon\"]": {
      "$description": "Named `state-icon` rather than `icon`: `jx-button` puts `part=\"icon\"` on the glyph slot of every button it draws, and the action button below is inside this same light-DOM tree — a rule on the bare name would reach into the kit's own drawing and a devtools query could not tell the two apart.",
      "flex": "none",
      "width": "14px",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "fontWeight": "700",
      "lineHeight": "1.5"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-state=\"running\"] > [part=\"state-icon\"]": {
      "color": "var(--accent)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"][data-state=\"done\"] > [part=\"state-icon\"]": {
      "color": "var(--success)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row-body\"]": {
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "alignItems": "flex-start",
      "gap": "2px"
    },
    "& [part=\"head\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "baseline",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-2)",
      "alignSelf": "stretch",
      "minWidth": "0"
    },
    "& [part=\"row-title\"]": {
      "fontWeight": "700",
      "overflow": "hidden",
      "textOverflow": "ellipsis",
      "whiteSpace": "nowrap"
    },
    "& [part=\"source\"]": {
      "$description": "Pushed to the far edge, so the tab reads as a column of who raised what.",
      "flex": "none",
      "marginLeft": "auto",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-sm)"
    },
    "& [part=\"summary\"]": {
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "overflowWrap": "anywhere"
    },
    "& [part=\"steps\"]": {
      "$description": "The chain, declared up front, so \"which link is missing\" is answered by looking rather than by reading the summary and remembering what came before it.",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "gap": "1px",
      "margin": "2px 0 0",
      "padding": "0",
      "listStyle": "none",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-sm)"
    },
    "& [part=\"step\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "gap": "6px",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [part=\"step\"][data-state=\"done\"] > [part=\"step-icon\"]": {
      "color": "var(--success)"
    },
    "& [part=\"step-icon\"]": {
      "flex": "none",
      "width": "10px",
      "textAlign": "center"
    },
    "& [part=\"action\"]": {
      "marginTop": "var(--jx-space-1)"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "tagName": "div",
      "attributes": {
        "part": "body-slot",
        "role": "none"
      },
      "style": {
        "display": "contents"
      },
      "$switch": {
        "$ref": "#/state/hasProject"
      },
      "cases": {
        "true": {
          "tagName": "ul",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "list"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "li",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "row",
                "data-state": "${state.rowState}"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "span",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "state-icon",
                    "aria-hidden": "true"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.rowIcon}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "div",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "row-body"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "div",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "head"
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tagName": "span",
                          "attributes": {
                            "part": "row-title"
                          },
                          "textContent": "Deploy checklist"
                        },
                        {
                          "tagName": "span",
                          "attributes": {
                            "part": "source"
                          },
                          "textContent": "Publish"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "div",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "summary"
                      },
                      "textContent": "${state.summary}"
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "ol",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "steps"
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "$prototype": "Array",
                          "items": {
                            "$ref": "#/state/steps"
                          },
                          "key": {
                            "$ref": "$map/item/id"
                          },
                          "map": {
                            "tagName": "li",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "step",
                              "data-step": "${$map.item.id}",
                              "data-state": "${$map.item.state}"
                            },
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "tagName": "span",
                                "attributes": {
                                  "part": "step-icon",
                                  "aria-hidden": "true"
                                },
                                "textContent": "${$map.item.icon}"
                              },
                              {
                                "tagName": "span",
                                "attributes": {
                                  "part": "step-text"
                                },
                                "textContent": "${$map.item.text}"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "span",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "action-slot",
                        "role": "none"
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "display": "contents"
                      },
                      "$switch": {
                        "$ref": "#/state/hasAction"
                      },
                      "cases": {
                        "true": {
                          "tagName": "jx-button",
                          "$description": "The recovery button wears the command's own title, so it reads as a verb rather than as a decoration, and a refused command is dimmed with the reason it names in its tooltip. A command the registry does not have, or whose `when` is false, draws NOTHING rather than a dead label — a surface may choose whether to show a command, never whether it exists (§12.4).",
                          "$props": {
                            "size": "sm",
                            "disabled": {
                              "$ref": "#/state/actionDisabled"
                            }
                          },
                          "attributes": {
                            "part": "action",
                            "title": "${state.actionTitle}"
                          },
                          "onclick": {
                            "$prototype": "Function",
                            "body": [
                              {
                                "operator": "call",
                                "target": {
                                  "$ref": "#/state/runAction"
                                },
                                "value": []
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "tagName": "span",
                              "textContent": "${state.actionLabel}"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
